senses
  entry
    definition "gain knowledge or skills"
    examples ("She learned dancing from her sister" "I learned Sanskrit" "Children acquire language at an amazing rate")
    id oewn-00599310-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (larn acquire)
  entry
    definition "get to know or become aware of, usually accidentally"
    examples ("I learned that she has two grown-up children" "I see that you have been promoted")
    id oewn-00600349-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (hear "get word" "get wind" "pick up" "find out" "get a line" discover see)
  entry
    definition "commit to memory; learn by heart"
    examples ("Have you memorized your lines for the play yet?")
    id oewn-00605971-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (memorize memorise con)
  entry
    definition "be a student of a certain subject"
    examples ("She is reading for the bar exam")
    id oewn-00601387-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (study read take)
  entry
    definition "impart skills or knowledge to"
    examples ("I taught them French" "He instructed me in building a boat")
    id oewn-00830768-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (teach instruct)
  entry
    definition "find out, learn, or determine with certainty, usually by making an inquiry or other effort"
    examples ("I want to see whether she speaks French" "See whether it works" "find out if he speaks Russian" "Check whether the train leaves on time")
    id oewn-00922307-v
    partOfSpeech v
    synonyms (determine check "find out" see ascertain watch)
